      "app_code": "APP-CONTROL",
      "app_name": "db_ops_control",
      "display_name": "Watch db_ops itself: alert on an app that starts failing, summarise every app hourly",
      "log_scope": "control",
      "working_dir": "tools/db_ops",
      "command_text": "python -m db_ops.db.cli ops-status '{\"mode\": \"auto\", \"telegram_chat\": \"control\", \"summary_from_hour\": 8, \"summary_to_hour\": 20, \"summary_interval_seconds\": 3600, \"window_hours\": 24}'",
      "note": "The one app that watches the others, and the one that must not depend on them. It reads job_runs directly and resolves its own chat from telegram_groups.json, so an estate where every other app is failing is exactly the estate it still reports from. Runs around the clock every 60s: the failure alert fires the moment an app command goes from working to failing, at any hour, while the app-by-app summary is confined to 08:00-20:00 local and one per hour (both decided inside ops-status, not by this schedule). Added 2026-08-13 after a NameError stopped every scheduled SQL task for a day with nothing to notice it - see db_ops/db/ops_status.py.",
      "active": true,
      "time_window": {
        "from_year": null,
        "to_year": null,
        "from_month": null,
